\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. I Want a principal within 
\par Of jealous, godly fear,
\par A sensibility of sin,
\par A pain to feel it near.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. I want the first approach to feel
\par Of pride or fond desire,
\par To catch the wandering of my will,
\par And quench the kindling fire.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. That I from Thee no more may part,
\par No more Thy goodness grieve,
\par The filial awe, the fleshly heart,
\par The tender conscience, give.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Quick us the apple of an eye,
\par O God, my conscience make;
\par Awake my soul when sin is nigh,
\par And keep it still awake.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. O may the least omission pain
\par My well instructed soul,
\par And drive me to the blood again
\par Which makes the wounded whole.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

